<title>MEXICO: Pemex lowers jet fuel to 1,764 pesos/cubic meter.</title>
<headline>Pemex lowers jet fuel to 1,764 pesos/cubic meter.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's state-owned oil and gas monopoly Petroleos Mexicanos (Pemex) said Tuesday it lowered its jet fuel prices to 1,764.42 pesos per cubic meter from its previous price of 1,838.25 pesos.</p>
<p>The average price of jet fuel has risen from 1,253.50 pesos per cubic meter on Jan. 2, 1996, Pemex said in a statement.</p>
<p>((--Timna Tanners, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-7903))</p>
